Patches applied by generator.go on top of the CPython 3.14 sources before
transpiling with ccgo.

pyexpat: ccgo rejects the tentative declaration `handler_info[64]` followed
by the definition `handler_info[] = { 23 entries + sentinel }` as conflicting
array types (clang only warns). Size both the same.

pycore_runtime_init.h / pycore_parser.h / action_helpers.c: ccgo emits a
pointer instead of an array literal for `uint8_t _data[N] = (LITERAL)` when
the string literal is parenthesized, and miscomputes the layout of a
designated union-member initializer (`.v.Name.id = ...`) inside a static
struct initializer. Drop the parentheses; set dummy_name's union fields at
runtime instead.

pyport.h / sre.c: ccgo drops the body of some `static inline` functions it
fails to inline (sre_lib.h SRE(match) is recursive; stringlib
SubString_new_object), leaving undefined references. Make CPython's
local-inline macros plain statics.
